w22-spec-satisficing
--------------------

This directory is a clean-room Python 3 standard-library method sketch. It is
original work for this repository and contains no third-party code, data or
weights.

Paper (method idea credited)
----------------------------
Ruixin Wang and Tianyi Zhang.
"Eliciting and Mitigating Specification Satisficing in Coding Agents".
arXiv:2611.16289, v1, submitted 12 Nov 2026 (2026-11-12 13:42:55 KST).
Primary category cs.SE, cross-listed cs.AI and cs.CL. SatisFix is the
method's name in the abstract, not the title.
https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.16289
Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ (a paper licence, not a
software grant).

Code: the abs page links no code repository. None was found or used.

Method only: the idea that an agent reports each implementation choice
with its reason and then checks each choice against the task description,
and that a self-correction step may favor a choice the`agent already
accepted. The commit gate, its order (report, then check, then commit),
the rule that a self-correction voids every earlier check, the fixture
labels, the oracle and the fixtures are this sketch's own rules, not the
paper's. No text, figures, tables or data from the paper are copied into
the code; the PDF was not read; no agent, model or benchmark was run. The
paper's claims appear only in paper_evidence.json, quoted and marked
UNVERIFIED.
